## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- lt-a row 5. “Kai kuriuose nuosprendžiuose” and “tipiškos ar garantuotos baigties nėra” are the R3 advertising softening, not a mistranslation. Restoring “teismai šiuo metu paprastai skiria … laisvės atėmimą” would put a usual criminal result back into the column.
- lt-a row 10 and lt-b row 26. Lithuanian normally groups thousands with a space, but this checker only accepts dot grouping for lt. Space separators were not introduced.
- lt-a row 11 and lt-b row 11. The one-line fragments and U+200B lines match the Korean source’s block and ZWSP counts. They are layout inherited from the source, not Lithuanian-only corruption. Making Q16 a heading, or deleting the zero-width spaces, fails check-column-translation.
- lt-b row 12. The jump from heading 5 to 7 is in the English source as well. Renumbering would change digits.
- lt-a row 21. “TWD 1.57M” is a pinned bio token. “1,57 mln. TWD” would break that test.
- lt-b row 24’s suggested sentence merges three source blocks into one. The calque was rewritten so the next block continues the sentence; the “Jei pradedate…” and “Jei sunku…” lines were left because they are the same English line breaks and are already grammatical Lithuanian.
